# Line endings: store and check out every text file with LF (the Linux/Mac style), on every machine.
# Why: Windows uses CRLF. Without this, a Windows commit can make every line of a file look changed,
#      and Git warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF". CI runs on Linux, so LF everywhere keeps them equal.
# text=auto: Git decides which files are text; binary files (images, zips) are left alone.
# Example: you save a file on Windows with CRLF; `git add` stores it with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
